000200 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000300 PROGRAM-ID.  TCORRCVR.
000400 AUTHOR.      JIM COFFMAN.
000600
000700*C************************************************************
000800*C                                                           *
000900*C  T C O R R C V R    THIS PROGRAMS PLACES ALL THE ENTRIES  *
001000*C    IN 'CORPFIL2' BACK INTO THE MCORPREQ DATASET. THIS     *
001100*C    PROGRAM IS USED FOR RECOVERY PURPOSES IN CASE THE      *
001200*C    CORPORATE REQ CREATE PROGRAM 'TREQABST' BLOWS DOWN     *
001300*C    BEFORE COMPLETELY PROCESSING THE CORPFILE ENTRIES.     *
001400*C    'FILE CORPRCVR=CORPFIL2' IS NEEDED TO POINT TO THE     *
001500*C    CORRECT FILE.                                          *
001600*C************************************************************
      *
      *C  01/06/00   CA YODER
      *C    ADDED LINE TO MOVE RELEASE NUMBER AS WELL BACK TO
      *C    MCORPREQ.
001700
001800 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
001900 CONFIGURATION SECTION.
002000 SOURCE-COMPUTER.  IBM-AS400.
002100 OBJECT-COMPUTER.  IBM-AS400.
002200
002300 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
002400 FILE-CONTROL.
002500     SELECT CORP-FIL2 ASSIGN TO DISK-CORPFIL2.
002600
           SELECT MCORPREQ-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS5701
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                  ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                      WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

002700 DATA DIVISION.
002800 FILE SECTION.
002900
003000 FD  CORP-FIL2
003100     LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED
003200     RECORD CONTAINS 20 CHARACTERS.
003300 01  CORP-FIL2-RCD.
003400     05  CF2-MCORPREQ-NUMBER      PIC X(12).
003500     05  CF2-MCORPREQ-STATUS      PIC XX.
003600*****05  FILLER                   PIC X(6).
           05  CF2-MCORPREQ-RLSE        PIC X(6).
003700
       FD  MCORPREQ-O
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MCORPREQ-REC-O.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS  OF MCFLCS5701.

003800 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
005500 77  PROCEED-SW                   PIC X(1)  VALUE SPACES.
005600 77  RCD-CTR                      PIC 9(4)  VALUE ZEROS.
004000
       01  FILE-STATUS.
           05  FILE-STATUS-1            PIC X  VALUE "0".
           05  FILE-STATUS-2            PIC X  VALUE "0".
005800
004100**************************************************************
004200**************************************************************
004300**                                                          **
004400**                DATABASE I/O BUFFER AREA                  **
004500**                                                          **
004600**************************************************************
004700**************************************************************
004800
004900 COPY MCORPREQ IN COPYLIB.
005000
005100*********************
005200*                   *
005300*   DATA SET NAMES  *
005400*                   *
005500*********************
005600
005700 01  DSET-NAMES.
005900     05  DSET-MCORPREQ          PIC X(16)  VALUE "MCORPREQ;".
006000
006100 COPY DATAB IN COPYLIB.
006200
006300 01 ITEMS-LISTING.
006400     05  ALL-ITEMS              PIC XX    VALUE "@;".
006500
006600 COPY TBLOWUP IN COPYLIB.
006700
006800 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
007300 1-BEGIN.
008000     OPEN I-O MCORPREQ-O.
007500     PERFORM 6-MAIN THRU 6-M-X.
008900     CLOSE MCORPREQ-O.
007700     GOBACK.
007800
009600*********************************************
009700*                                           *
009800*  BLOWUP ROUTINE EXECUTES WHENEVER A       *
009900*  FATAL ERROR OCCURS                       *
010000*                                           *
010100*********************************************
010200
010300 2-BLOWUP.
010400     MOVE  "TCORRCVR"     TO  BU-PGM-NAME.
010500     CALL "TBLOWUP" USING BASE, BU-PGM-NAME, STATUS-AREA,
010600         DUMMY-VIEW-AREA, DUMMY-KSAM-STAT, BU-DISPLAY-MSG,
010700                 BU-DISPLAY-FLDS.
010900 2-BLOWUP-X.    EXIT.
011100
011200**************************************************
011300*                                                *
011400*     6 - M A I N                                *
011500*                                                *
011600**************************************************
011700
011800 6-MAIN.
017700     DISPLAY "THE FILE USED AS INPUT IS 'CORPFIL2'.  IF THIS".
017800     DISPLAY "IS NOT THE DESIRED FILE YOU MUST ENTER A".
           DISPLAY "OVERRIDE DATA BASE FILE 'OVRDBF'".
017900     DISPLAY "STATEMENT BEFORE RUNNING THIS PROGRAM!!!".
018500     DISPLAY "  ".
018600     DISPLAY "OK TO PROCEED 'N/Y'?".
018700     ACCEPT  PROCEED-SW.
018800     DISPLAY "  ".
018900     IF PROCEED-SW = "Y"
019000         DISPLAY "*** STARTING RECOVERY!!! ***"
019100     ELSE
019200     DISPLAY "*** NO PROCESSING DONE!!! ***"
019300     GO TO 6-M-X.
019400
011900     OPEN INPUT CORP-FIL2.
012000     PERFORM 61-READ-CORPFIL2          THRU  61-RC-X.
012100     CLOSE CORP-FIL2.
019800     DISPLAY "*** RECOVERY COMPLETE !!! ***".
019900     DISPLAY RCD-CTR,
020000      " ENTRIES WERE PLACED BACK INTO - 'MCORPREQ'."             .
012300 6-M-X.    EXIT.
012500
012600 61-READ-CORPFIL2.
013400     READ CORP-FIL2 AT END
013500         GO TO 61-RC-X.
013700     MOVE SPACES                  TO  BUF-MCORPREQ.
013800     MOVE CF2-MCORPREQ-NUMBER     TO  MCORPREQ-REQ-NUMBER.
013900     MOVE CF2-MCORPREQ-STATUS     TO  MCORPREQ-REQ-STATUS.
           MOVE CF2-MCORPREQ-RLSE       TO  MCORPREQ-RLSE.
014200     WRITE MCORPREQ-REC-O FROM BUF-MCORPREQ
014300         INVALID KEY MOVE FILE-STATUS TO FILE-STATUS.
014400     IF FILE-STATUS NOT = "00"
014500         MOVE "PUT MCORPREQ*61-RC" TO BU-DISPLAY-MSG
014600         GO TO 2-BLOWUP.
           ADD 1                        TO  RCD-CTR.
014800     GO TO 61-READ-CORPFIL2.
015700 61-RC-X.    EXIT.
